rows.translation_en:
@You won't be able to choose Sortie or Rest,
so please keep that in mind
when planning your month.

@Buy / Sell is for buying and selling items!!
You only have to give the orders here, %$.
I'll run into town to do the shopping.

@At least once a year, let's clear out
all that junk gathering dust in the storehouse
and sell it off with a bang!

@You can't sell weapons or armor anyone is wearing.
We couldn't have someone catching a cold
because their clothes suddenly vanished!

@Um, and as for shopping,
you'll need to invest quite a bit
before the shops are any use at all.

@Thanks to Shuten, the capital is in ruins.
There isn't a single shop
with a decent selection!

@But don't worry!!
I'll put my heart into making equipment
for your children's first battles.

@Facilities lets you visit various places
besides the weapon shop, armor shop
and general store.

@As life returns to the capital,
we should get more useful services
and more ridiculous little extras too.

@Ridiculous little extras!!
Doesn't that sound fun?
I can hardly wait!

@Rebuild lets you invest in restoring
the beauty and bustle of this capital
after Shutendoji's rampage.

@And for that, above all, we need money!!
Good intentions and stirring slogans
won't get people moving, will they?

@More shops mean more goods!!
Skilled craftspeople and pretty young women
will come flocking here too!!

@Exactly!! You're not throwing money away.
It'll come back around one day,
many times over, with a bang!

@Rest lets the whole family
spend a month relaxing at home,
recovering strength for tomorrow.

@You can still buy, sell, invest in rebuilding
and read reports,
but you can't perform Divine Union or set out.

@Incidentally, anyone who isn't chosen
for Divine Union or a sortie
rests on their own anyway.

@Well, once in a while, why not have everyone
gather around the low table
and enjoy a nice meal together!?

@Save records your current progress.
You can create
only one set of save data!!

@Whatever happens, save only once a day
and avoid resetting as much as you can.
That's the spirit I'd like you to play in!!

@The Pack doesn't hold all that much,
but it's wonderfully handy:
you can take it straight out on a sortie.

@The Storehouse is... well, a storehouse!!
You can keep mountains of items in it,
but you certainly can't carry it around...

@When you return from a hunt, sort out
your loot-filled Pack before you forget.
Toss anything you won't need soon into storage!

@Help gives rather slapdash explanations
of this world's special terms and systems,
along with some rather unreliable advice.

@So when you're feeling stuck,
I'd be delighted if you read it for a laugh,
a little comfort, or just to pass the time!

@Settings includes text display speed,
switching between the play-time modes,
and so on and so forth.

@Births, new clan heads taking office,
victories over powerful enemies...
The Chronicle is the history of the %@ clan.

@But since the one writing it is me,
the world's least detail-minded person,
hee-hee...

@So, %$, I'd recommend keeping
your own history of the %@ clan
in your own words!!

@The party leader's job is very important,
so please remember
what I'm about to tell you!!

@First: when you aren't joining a sortie, %$,
please appoint someone you trust
to lead the party.

@Second: during battle, everyone except the leader
will regularly suggest
three tactics of their own.

@You can reject those suggestions,
but please try to choose one when possible
to encourage their initiative.

@Third: if the leader can no longer fight,
the party retreats at once, even if the others are fine.
Keep a close eye on the leader's HP.

@For Best Equipment, I hand things out
in the order you selected the party,
judging only by the equipment's numbers.

@You shouldn't worry either, %$.
Fussing over every little thing
will make you go bald!

@Before your first sortie,
please allow me, %$,
to offer some advice.

@Until you're used to the tactics of battle,
don't skimp on medicine. Heal your HP early,
while you still have plenty to spare.

@If you meet an unexpectedly powerful enemy,
use your last resort under Skills:
the Clan Head's Ring.

@If you're stuck in a dungeon
with no way out, choose Return.
Well, do your best!!
